      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{log}_{3}⁡(4-2x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{3}⁡(4-2x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246608/assets/b1d65d2df4e6a5a6b66e908ed8f776e2a1b8a4b24896506d3625e6569d9ea4e6.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\ge 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}{log}_{3}⁡(4-2x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x<2.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{log}_{3}⁡(4-2x)=-\\infty .\n$$",
